# Why: Lazy-load contract for Supabase JS is documented in app.jsx:18-22 + the
#      ensureSupabase() helper at app.jsx:48 — every anonymous visitor is
#      supposed to skip the ~80KB gzipped UMD bundle until they tap Sign in or
#      land on a magic-link redirect. The eager <script> tag in index.html
#      (lines 83-85) defeats this and ships ~80KB to every cold load. Same
#      finding as devops-2026-05-06.md §P1-eager. Day 2 unchanged, Rule 1
#      spirit applies (delete-block, scoped, low risk).
# Estimated time to apply: 30 seconds (git apply + bump cache stamp)
# Risk: low — deletes 3 lines in one file, ensureSupabase() already
#       handles the cold-load injection path. Bump CACHE_NAME +
#       PEAKLY_BUILD + index.html ?v= in lockstep to 20260508a so
#       service workers mid-fetch get fresh HTML.

--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -80,10 +80,6 @@
   <script crossorigin src="https://unpkg.com/react@18.3.1/umd/react.production.min.js"></script>
   <script crossorigin src="https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18.3.1/umd/react-dom.production.min.js"></script>

